# THE SITE'S FRAMES (unspent.world, site/frames/): the moments the landing page
# shows, each taken with the slate's edge hidden so the frame is the world alone.
# Not a proof: a camera. tools/site/frames.py turns what it shoots into the
# page's images; run both again when the look moves on.
#
#   TOUR_TIMEOUT=900 TOUR_FIXED_FPS=60 tools/tour.sh tours/site.tour --scene=title --seed=1
# Options: --scene=title --seed=1
#
# From the title as a player starts (home-coast.tour's opening), for the wake and
# the first sight of the Tether, which only a new game stages.
await title 40
tap use
await character 8
key move_up
key use
await game 120
hud hidden
await waking 5
wait 0.4
hud hidden
shot 01-surf with waking
await woken 10
await staging:tether 6
wait 1.2
hud hidden
shot 02-tether with staging:tether
wait 4.0
# What's left of the town by day, from above, then over his shoulder: the rest
# is shot from there, the view a player turns to for a look round.
coast calm
at cast:maren
hour 10
wait 1.0
hud hidden
shot 03-town with cast:maren
tap shoulder
await shoulder 20
wait 1.2
hud hidden
shot 04-town-shoulder with shoulder
# The Tide Reaper at its work, under a low sun.
near keeper
hour 17
wait 1.5
hud hidden
shot 05-reaper with shoulder
# The drowned city at the end of the afternoon.
place drowned_city
hour 17.5
wait 1.5
hud hidden
shot 06-drowned with shoulder,land:drowned_city
# The coast's open water at dusk.
place coast
hour 19.2
wait 1.5
hud hidden
shot 07-coast-dusk with shoulder,land:coast
# The town after dark, its fire and lamps.
at cast:maren
hour 21.5
wait 1.5
hud hidden
shot 08-town-night with shoulder
# The crew's camp after dark, last: it stages by Rook, who may not stand there
# yet on a new game, and a staging that fails ends the run after every frame above.
at cast:rook
wait 1.5
hud hidden
shot 09-camp-night with shoulder,cast:rook
